                &lt;div&gt;
                    
                        &lt;article&gt;
                            &lt;h2&gt;&lt;a href="https://github.com/open-telemetry/opentelemetry-dotnet-contrib/releases/tag/Exporter.InfluxDB-1.0.0-alpha.11"&gt;Exporter.InfluxDB-1.0.0-alpha.11&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
                            &lt;div&gt;
                                &lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;p&gt;NuGet: &lt;a href="https://www.nuget.org/packages/OpenTelemetry.Exporter.InfluxDB/1.0.0-alpha.11" rel="nofollow"&gt;OpenTelemetry.Exporter.InfluxDB v1.0.0-alpha.11&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Write metrics synchronously and report &lt;code&gt;ExportResult.Failure&lt;/code&gt; when a write to&lt;br&gt;
InfluxDB fails, so the SDK applies backpressure instead of growing an unbounded&lt;br&gt;
in-memory buffer while InfluxDB is unavailable. The &lt;code&gt;FlushInterval&lt;/code&gt; option is&lt;br&gt;
deprecated as it no longer applies.&lt;br&gt;
(&lt;a href="https://github.com/open-telemetry/opentelemetry-dotnet-contrib/pull/4861" data-hovercard-type="pull_request" data-hovercard-url="/open-telemetry/opentelemetry-dotnet-contrib/pull/4861/hovercard"&gt;#4861&lt;/a&gt;)&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;See &lt;a href="https://github.com/open-telemetry/opentelemetry-dotnet-contrib/blob/Exporter.InfluxDB-1.0.0-alpha.11/src/OpenTelemetry.Exporter.InfluxDB/CHANGELOG.md"&gt;CHANGELOG&lt;/a&gt; for details.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
                            &lt;/div&gt;
